  "description": "If you dream of bikepacking, you dream of the Unity. It’s a mountain bike that was built to carry more, wander farther, and keep going when cell service is long, long gone. Mixed wheels and big tires keep it planted and capable, while load-optimized geometry keeps the ride predictable when you’ve packed everything but the kitchen sink. An oversized front triangle leaves plenty of room for a proper frame bag, and the custom integrated front cargo rack is ready for the rest. Load it up for a week in the mountains. Strip it down and rip your local trails. Build the off-grid battle cruiser of your dreams. Mountain bike, gravel bike, touring machine… The Unity doesn’t really care—it just wants to go.",
